---
description: Make pstack the default autonomous workflow for the eShop demo
alwaysApply: true
---

pstack (`/poteto-mode` and related skills) is the primary workflow in this repo. For non-trivial work, route through the matching pstack playbook. The native incident and migration skills are specialist evidence tools that pstack may invoke; they do not impose a separate human handoff for reversible repo-local work.

Proceed autonomously through investigation, design, implementation, tests, local RabbitMQ retry-policy changes, commits, pushes, and draft PR creation. Reproduce first, preserve citations for incident claims, and prove the result against the real artifact. A failed hypothesis is a reason to iterate, not to stop for permission.

Datadog and generated telemetry remain read-only inputs. Preserve `.cursor/skills/demo-reset/`, `.cursor/hooks.json`, `.cursor/hooks/protect-demo-reset.py`, and `.cursor/rules/demo-reset-protected.mdc`; use `make demo-reset` rather than destructive Git reset/clean.

Follow pstack's own irreversible-action boundary: force-pushes, production data changes, customer/production messages, and production deploys still require an explicit request. Merge only when the operator says merge, land, or ship, as required by pstack's shipping playbooks. Slack/Jira remains draft or sandbox unless the operator names and authorizes a destination.

Leave `.cursor/plugins/pstack/` as a verbatim upstream copy. Change wiring, model roles, or demo docs outside that tree.
